#### Live preview

Open the Markdown preview pane with: 
 - `Ctrl+Shift+V` - replacing the editor view.
 - `Ctrl+K V` - to the side - as you type in the editor, the preview updates in real time. This is invaluable for checking table alignment, verifying image paths, and seeing exactly how your step will look when published.

> **Tip:** The live preview and IntelliSense work together. Use the preview to see the rendered result, and IntelliSense to insert variable references without errors.


#### Spell checking as you type

VS Code doesn't include spell checking out of the box - to add it, you'll need to install an extension. We recommend **Code Spell Checker**, which underlines misspelled words with a subtle squiggle as you write. It understands **Markdown** natively, skipping code blocks and URLs automatically.

To take it a step further, we provide a `.cspell.json` configuration file and setup instructions. This extends the checker to ignore all **Docs Assembler** specific elements as well,.

So you'll see flags only on your actual prose, never on the underlying machinery.


##### Code Spell Checker

The extension itself is installed once globally for VS Code. But you'll need to configure it separately for each repository to activate custom settings. 

